            "created_at": "2025-09-01T03:28:37.074629+00:00",
            "notes": "Start with \"Phantasm\" to spawn a stationary orb when fading. The orb spawned is the last orb thrown, so it is important to time this with your regular Biotic Orb use. You can do this by ensuring that you can always support your team with an orb - whether through fading or throwing one. That being said, you should always have either your fade or biotic orb available and interchange these cooldowns.\nThis build is the best when you have a tank who has some sort of shield (rein, orisa, sigma, etc.) so you can front line with them while protecting yourself and close-range healing them. I will ALWAYS make sure that when I fade, I will spawn a healing orb, and I will fade backwards from my tank. This ensures they have a healing orb nearby, and if they needs more support, I can always throw a Biotic Orb after fading behind them.\n\nNote: If you do not have a tank who has a shield, stay back with a dps or support who cannot dive. It will help to protect them as well as yourself, and you can fade forwards to help your team - leaving the faded orb with a hero who has less movement abilities.",
